  "slides": [
    {
      "id": "slide-1",
      "name": "Title",
      "background": "#ffffff",
      "notes": "Thirteen years of the whole 311 record — not a sample. 32,502,367 rows, 1 Jan 2010 to 12 Mar 2023.\n\nSay the number out loud, then get off this slide."
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-2",
      "name": "The scale",
      "notes": "Five clicks: one per KPI, then the takeaway.\n\nSELECT COUNT(*), COUNT(DISTINCT complaint_type), COUNT(DISTINCT agency) FROM sample_data.nyc.service_requests;\n  -> 32502367 / 484 / 34. 6,746 a day is that total over the 4,818 days spanned.\n47.3% is the share with a closed_date inside 24 hours of created_date."
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-3",
      "name": "Section: channels",
      "background": "#fbf7f0",
      "notes": "Breath. The next slide is the one chart people remember, so land the sentence before you show it."
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-4",
      "name": "Channel mix",
      "notes": "Two clicks: the chart, then the callout.\n\nPhone peaked at 1,480,750 in 2018 and fell to 782,393 in 2022. Online went 166,403 (2012) -> 1,437,656 (2022) and crossed phone in 2021.\nStarts in 2012 on purpose — see the backup slide.\n\nSELECT strftime(created_date,'%Y') AS yr, ... GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1"
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-5",
      "name": "What gets reported",
      "notes": "The grid is live: it runs at load, so the numbers are whatever the table says today.\n\nTop eight sum to 38.9%. Noise — Residential alone is 9.3% (3,006,824).\nClusters: noise 9.3+3.2; heat/heating/plumbing 6.0+2.7+2.7; parking 5.9+4.2."
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-6",
      "name": "How fast it closes",
      "notes": "NYPD's median is 0.0 days on 5.6M requests — a noise call is closed by the responding officer's shift.\nDPR 12.3 days with 24.6% still open; TLC 42.2 days with 24.7% still open.\nEleven agencies clear the 100,000-request floor, so the grid draws all of them.\n\nWindow is 2018-2022 so the pandemic years are in and the partial 2023 is out."
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-7",
      "name": "Backup: method",
      "notes": "Hidden, so present mode skips it and the counter reads 7 slides, not 8. Jump here from the filmstrip if someone asks about the 2012 start or the duplicate heat labels.",
      "hidden": true
    },
    {
      "id": "slide-8",
      "name": "Closing",
      "background": "#ffffff",
      "notes": "Phone 2018 1,480,750 -> 2022 782,393 = -47.2%. Total 2018 2,760,103 -> 2022 3,169,759 = +14.8%. Stop there."
    }
  ],
